' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads data members and nothing else. A class whose
' behaviour lives in methods arrives as a box holding only its private state,
' a facet of free functions does not arrive at all, and static and using
' members are skipped. The blocks below fill those boxes and draw the
' relationships the automated pass cannot see.
'
' They use fully-qualified class names rather than a reopened namespace block,
' because this PlantUML version crashes when a namespace that already holds
' classes is declared a second time. Redeclaring a class merges its members
' into the box the automated pass already drew, so a refresh keeps both.

note top of "ores::synthetic::domain::folder"
The automated pass drops three things. It drops every method. It drops a
static or using member. It drops a declaration that wraps onto a second
line. A fourth defect -- it dropped any member whose initialiser or trailing
comment carried a parenthesis, which caught tenant_id on all nine generated
entities and the spot and year-fraction members of the feed context -- is
fixed at source in this pass, so those members now arrive from the automated
pass too and the redeclarations below merge with them. The wrapped members,
such as fx_spot_feed_build_input.binding_mode and the EAV optionals, are
restored by hand.
end note

note right of "ores::synthetic::domain::folder"
Generic self-referencing hierarchy node, one root folder per party. The
