class ores::synthetic::domain::curve_template_validation {
    {static} +validate_curve_template(entries : vector<curve_template_entry_ref>, tenors : vector<tenor>, convention : tenor_convention, resolutions : vector<tenor_convention_resolution>, horizon : date, spot : date) : curve_template_validation_result
}
note right of "ores::synthetic::domain::curve_template_validation"
Free function, hand-written. It rejects a Curve Template when two entries'
resolved tenor periods genuinely overlap: an interval instrument (an FRA,
start_tenor_code other than SPOT) must not overlap another interval's period,
and must not contain another entry's maturity. Point instruments (deposits and
swaps, start_tenor_code SPOT) contribute only their maturity, so two of them
never collide by construction. Touching endpoints are legal, because a
bootstrappable strip is built from back-to-back periods. It never throws: a
failed tenor resolution comes back as the message in
curve_template_validation_result.
end note

