}
note top of "ores::synthetic::domain::yield_curve_process_parameter_mapping"
Free function, hand-written. It joins a config's {parameter_definition_id,
value} rows onto the system-tenant definitions catalogue and constructs the
matching ores.analytics.quant process. It throws std::invalid_argument on an
unknown process type, an unknown or foreign definition id, a repeated
parameter, a missing required parameter, an undeclared parameter, or a value
outside the definition's [min_value, max_value]. That range check is why the
catalogue's bounds are load-bearing and not display metadata.
end note

