note top of "ores::synthetic::feed::ir_curve_template_resolver"
Free functions in ir_curve_template_resolver.hpp, hand-written. resolve()
turns raw (tenor code, instrument code) template rows into tick counts, year
fractions, and fixed-leg schedules. Its conventions are deliberate Phase-1
simplifications: one tick is one calendar day, spot equals the horizon (T+0),
and year fractions are Actual/365. The refdata context is built once at feed
construction and never touched by the tick loop: resolve once, tick many.
price_ir_curve_entry() is shared by the feed's tick loop and by the stateless
shape-preview handler, so the two can never disagree on a rate.
end note

